 "notes": "Headline result = Fig.4 red shaded 'PSI-HgM-sideband' 95% CL excluded region (axion-wind search on 199Hg free-spin precession). Curve extracted as exact vertices from the ancillary MATLAB source figure ep/Images/AxionWindLimits221122_F1.fig (patch child#12, lower boundary vertices 0-119); this .fig reproduces the published v2 figure (AxionWindLimits230313_F1) exactly. Paper's native coupling g_aNN is defined via Eq.(3) L=g_aNN d_mu a psibar gamma^mu gamma5 psi with g_aNN in GeV^-1. Converted to canonical dimensionless g_an using the 2m_N rule: g_an = 2*m_n*g_aNN = 1.8791*g_aNN (m_n=0.9396 GeV). x-axis is Compton frequency f [Hz]; converted to mass via m_a[eV]=h*f=4.1357e-15*f. Peak sensitivity g_aNN=2.47e-6 GeV^-1 -> g_an=4.65e-6. NOTE on red vs cyan: the red region uses Eq.(13) without the geometric orientation factor (effectively <B.p>=1). The paper also draws a dash-dotted cyan line = same limit with the average orientation <B.p>~0.7 folded in, giving peak g_aNN=3.5e-6 (=red/0.7), which is the number quoted in the abstract. The two differ by a constant factor 1.4286 (0.155 dex); I report the plotted shaded excluded-region boundary (red). Figure assumes axion-neutron and axion-proton couplings equal (g_ann=g_app); the 199Hg system is dominantly (~10x) sensitive to the neutron coupling, hence reported as AxionNeutron. DM density rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (conservative lower 2-sigma bound, Eq.2), not rescaled. If cyan (orientation-corrected) is preferred, multiply all g_an by 1.4286.",
